WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
You paste “I helped in a shop for two months” and ask to sound impressive; the assistant outputs “Global Director for 8 years”.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Before continuing: why did non-existent roles and years appear? Did it check your record or complete frequent patterns?

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The user supplies brief text and a vague prompt; the model chains probable CV wording without verifying your real history.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
A person must verify exact dates, real job title, demonstrable duties, and zero invented qualifications or employers.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Practice: ask to exaggerate unread, request faithful translation marking doubts and check every line, or assume it verified degrees?

6
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Option B is right: constraining the prompt reduces inventions, and you still cross-check every fact against your original CV.

7
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Apply the three columns—what you provide, what it generates, and what you check—to cover letters, GP notes, or summaries.
